│ More than 30 percent of patients with epilepsy have inadequate control of seizures with drug therapy, but why this   │
│ happens and whether it can be predicted are unknown. We studied the response to antiepileptic drugs in patients with │
│ newly diagnosed epilepsy to identify factors associated with subsequent poor control of seizures.   Methods We       │
