│ was developed and applied to the trials assessed in a large, unselected cohort of Cochrane systematic reviews.       │
│ Researchers who conducted the trials were contacted and the reason sought for the non-reporting of data. A           │
│ sensitivity analysis was undertaken to assess the impact of outcome reporting bias on reviews that included a single │
│ meta-analysis of the review primary outcome.Results More than half (157/283 (55%)) the reviews did not include full  │
│ data for the review primary outcome of interest from all eligible trials. The median amount of review outcome data   │
